About cmsdk_apb_uart
---

Accroding to DDI0479B $4.3.1, the register interface of cmsdk_apb_uart includes:
- DATA
- STATE
- CTRL
- INTSTATUS/INTCLEAR
- BAUDDIV

Other registers are all read-only.

In these registers, only below 2 are read-only:
- STATE[0] TX buffer full
- STATE[1] RX buffer full

All the others must be written 1 to clear.

So this implies STATE[0]/[1] are maintained by the hardware.
And we have to rely on them to determine if there's data to Tx or Rx.
And this true as I experimented.

After we act according to the STATE[0]/[1], we can write 1 to clear
other related registers.
